Every recorded call and the machine-code boundary it crosses
=============================================================

This inventory follows the actual CALL instructions in the source archive.
Every call is included whether or not the sample data executed it.
A direct address visible in the linked executable is distinguished from
an object-file relocation, a linker trampoline and an unknown indirect
target. A symbol name is not a machine-state proof of the called body.

External routines: dnrm2_, dscal_, ddot_, daxpy_, dcopy_ are BLAS
numerical-library entry points; memmove/memset are C memory-library
entries. The archived linked executable does not include their shared
library implementations. Those uninspected instructions cannot be
invented in English. PLT stubs also require dynamic linker state.

Known source-based call purposes are supplied only as annotations
after the machine boundary, not used to fabricate execution traces.

